  "narrative": {
    "intro": "FY2027 to date federal contract obligations in Illinois total $691M. The federal government executed 23,986 awards in the state, with an average award size of $28.8K. Obligations fell 94.8% year over year. Prior full fiscal years show much larger totals: FY22 obligations were $13.7B, FY23 obligations were $13.5B, FY24 obligations were $14.4B, FY25 obligations were $13B, and FY26 obligations were $13.2B. The FY27 total of $691M is the partial, fiscal year to date figure. Agency buying is concentrated, led by the Department of Energy with $289M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $259M. Vendor payments are concentrated as well, led by FERMI FORWARD DISCOVERY GROUP, LLC with $173M and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC with $116M. Research-related industries top the NAICS list, led by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) with $175M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences with $116M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY27 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY27 to date obligations are $691M, a marked decline from recent full fiscal years. FY22 obligations were $13.7B, FY23 obligations were $13.5B, FY24 obligations were $14.4B, FY25 obligations were $13B, and FY26 obligations were $13.2B. Obligations fell 94.8% year over year. The FY27 figure is a partial, fiscal year to date total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for the most FY27 to date spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer with $289M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $259M. FERMI FORWARD DISCOVERY GROUP, LLC received $173M and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC received $116M. Research and development industries lead NAICS spending, with $175M and $116M in the top two R&D categories respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
