      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Illinois?",
      "a": "Illinois received $691M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 23,986 awards with an average award size of $28.8K, and obligations fell 94.8% year over year. Prior full fiscal years were much larger: FY22 $13.7B, FY23 $13.5B, FY24 $14.4B, FY25 $13B, and FY26 $13.2B."
